  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Polyisobutylene is a polymer molecule which is produced by the polymerization of isobutene (also known as 2-methylpropene). The chemical formula of isobutene is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Polymerization happens according to the following reaction:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/11488f48-c958-4d82-af69-89ae0c30156c-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 168px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
